     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi's family travelled to Rameswaram to take a holy dip.\n\"Many people travel to sacred places,\" said his father."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pilgrimage",
     "sacred",
     "shrine"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Many Indians treat rivers, mountains, trees and places as sacred. A pilgrimage is a journey to such a place, like Varanasi, Rameswaram, Bodh Gaya or Amritsar.\nSacred places are linked to stories, saints and festivals. People of different faiths visit places that matter to them.\nPilgrim routes link far-off parts of India and spread culture and trade."
    }
